course: dictionary
lesson: 1791
title: A cloche is a bell-shaped cover
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A cloche can mean three different things: a glass cover over young plants in a garden, a close-fitting hat from the 1920s, or a dome over a hot plate of food. To know which one a writer means, look at the clues around the word. In gardens, the clues are plants, seeds, cold and pests.
explain: The sentence «In France church bells are silent before Easter; children are told les cloches de Pâques fly to Rome» has different clues: church bells, Easter, silent and flying. Here cloches means bells. French uses the same word, so always check the words around it.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence. If a glass cover fits the garden, a dome fits dinner and a hat fits the 1920s, you have found the right one.
fact: A cloche is a bell-shaped cover.
fact: A garden cloche is a glass or plastic cover that protects young plants from cold and pests.
fact: A garden cloche works like a mini greenhouse: it traps warmth so seeds sprout earlier.
fact: In the 1920s, a close-fitting, bell-shaped woman's hat was called a cloche.
fact: A cloche over food is a dome-shaped cover that keeps the plate warm. In French, «cloche» means bell, as in «les cloches de Pâques».
exercise: «The young lettuces were covered with a glass cloche to keep off the frost.» What is a cloche here? | A kind of fish | *A glass cover that protects plants from the cold | A loud church bell ringing on Sunday | A brown paper bag for a picnic
exercise: «Flappers in the 1920s wore cloche hats.» Which best describes a cloche hat? | *A close-fitting, bell-shaped hat | A wide-brimmed hat for the beach | A tall top hat for a horse race | A woolly hat for snow
exercise: «The waiter lifted the silver cloche to reveal the warm dinner.» Where would you most likely find a cloche? | Inside a seed tray | *On a plate in a restaurant, keeping food warm | On a horse's head | In a bell tower on a church
test: In «les cloches de Pâques fly to Rome», what does cloches mean? | Dome covers for food | Hats | Glass covers for plants | *Bells
test: Why does a garden cloche help seeds sprout earlier? | *It keeps warmth in, like a mini greenhouse | It blows cold wind away from the seeds | It waters the seeds every day | It gives the seeds food
exam: Which of these is a cloche that keeps food warm? | A bell hanging in a church tower | *A dome-shaped cover over a hot plate | A glass cover over young seedlings | A close-fitting hat worn in the 1920s
